+(duration)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a span of time to a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole number
+of seconds, such as `120`, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups using the units `d` (days), `h` (hours), `m`
+(minutes), and `s` (seconds), such as `2d`, `90m`, `1h30m`, or `1d2h3m4s`. Units are case-insensitive. Each unit may
+be given at most once and in that order, without spaces. Negative and decimal values are not accepted. A
+{class}`~datetime.timedelta` passed as the default is used as is.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=120'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=30m1h'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+```
+
